sequenceDiagram
  %% A stopped nested-fleet clone's start on the Gateway engine: the steps of instance/start.mmd (workflow operation-instance-start) as executor primitives of the `instance` and `power` families, reusing those of instance.create. Design for ADR 0267 and ADR 0271; no engine flow exists yet. Step names describe effects; the implementation settles action names unless an existing action is named.
  %% The wake admits `instance.start` (instance/wake.mmd); this chart is placed beside instance/start.mmd on instance/wake.mdx.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:wake
  %% kind: instance.start
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=copy tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>executor
  participant C as Container<br/>via executor
  CLI->>GW: instance:wake INSTANCE
  Note over GW: Start or join the start<br/>one per Instance
  %%> Same admission as instance/start.mmd: an open start is joined; other work refuses (`operation.target_busy`, `instance.lifecycle_busy`); a nested-fleet default refuses (`instance.sleep_unsupported`)
  %%> The Club key is read once here; without one the start fails before any step (`instance.nested_club_key_missing`)
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `instance.start` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: `discard`, `instance.start`, `instance.club_key` and `instance.fleet_ready` (all exist), and the new container-state read, unit wait and marker removal actions
    %%> - `instance.start`'s decoder refuses unknown fields, so the new inputs below need evidence first: the Node lists a feature for them in its reported `features` (as `instance.t3_pairing`), else the whole start stays on Swamp; it never fails after earlier steps acted
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    %%> - eligible plan: a stopped clone whose seed holds Orbit's tunnel boot unit (`fleet_tunnel` recorded at create); a frozen copy (its wake resumes it) and a seed without the tunnel unit (Swamp's clone-fleet) throw `EngineUnsupported`
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    EN->>N: Read the container state<br/>Incus status · read-only
    N-->>EN: Stopped or Running
    opt Incus reports Stopped
      EN->>N: Discard the freeze plan<br/>power discard
      %%> A stopped copy's prepared plan and limits record go before the boot, under the Instance's target lock, as the Swamp start does
      %%> Skipped when the read finds the copy Running: `discard` refuses a running target, so a retry Operation after the boot never sends it
    end
    EN->>C: Start the copy<br/>instance.start · guard · names
    %%> Reuses `instance.start`: NIC guards and egress gates, the allowed config of a nested-fleet copy, ID maps, boot, hostname and `/etc/hosts`; an already running copy changes nothing
    %%> New inputs, behind the feature above: the start guard's owned keys `boot.autostart=false` and `limits.memory.swap` written over an absent or different value; the presented machine name; and, for a copy still Stopped, the recorded server's drop-in `/etc/systemd/system/t3.service.d/20-orbit-server.conf` before the boot, so t3.service starts the recorded server
    C-->>EN: Running<br/>applied
    EN->>C: Deliver the Club key<br/>instance.club_key · tmpfs
    %%> Into the copy's `/run`, never a seed or snapshot; answers changed, changed_serve_pending or unchanged
    EN->>C: Wait for the boot units<br/>FrankenPHP · boot Processes
    %%> As the Swamp start: reads the Process units that start at boot (installed and enabled) and FrankenPHP, then waits for each to be active with an empty `Job=`; a bounded read from the Node, failing `instance.container_start_failed` at the bound
    C-->>EN: Units active<br/>names · seconds
    EN->>N: Remove the asleep marker<br/>after the units answer
    %%> Right after the boot units are ready, before the fleet check, as the outer start phase does (instance-container-phase.yml `Remove the asleep marker after the start`): Caddy sends the next request to the running app; an absent marker counts as removed
    %%> A later fleet failure fails the Operation but never puts the app back behind the sleep gate; a failure before this step keeps the marker
    EN->>C: Wait for the fleet<br/>instance.fleet_ready · start
    %%> Readiness, as the Swamp start's fleet check: inner Incus, stopped nested containers started, the tunnel unit active, Doctor healthy over the tunnel, every agent online
    %%> `seed_without_tunnel` fails the step; the engine never hands the rest to Swamp
    C-->>EN: fleet ready<br/>started · fleet_seconds
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>C: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so Instance 42 stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
      C-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record running<br/>power_state · club key
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Record the failure<br/>power_state unchanged
      %%> - the container may run with a fleet that is not ready; retry: the same command, and each step leaves what already runs as it is
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-instance-start
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-instance-start (instance/start.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
